    {"id": 23, "text": "Folding consistently delivers fresher state by selecting smaller views when channel conditions constrain transmission, preventing deferral.", "poster_quote": "Folding consistently delivers fresher state by selecting smaller views when channel conditions constrain transmission, preventing deferral."},
    {"id": 24, "text": "OR-based folding maps canonical positions to folded space via modulo arithmetic: b’[i] = OR of all b[j] where j mod m’ = i.", "poster_quote": "OR-based folding maps canonical positions to folded space via modulo arithmetic: b’[i] = OR of all b[j] where j mod m’ = i."},
    {"id": 25, "text": "For non-integer ratios, membership query uses two-stage mapping: H_i(x) mod m (canonical), then mod m’ (folded).", "poster_quote": "For non-integer ratios, membership query uses two-stage mapping: H_i(x) mod m (canonical), then mod m’ (folded)."},
    {"id": 26, "text": "This preserves no-false-negative property.", "poster_quote": "This preserves no-false-negative property."},
    {"id": 27, "text": "FPR increases as retained ratio r = m’/m decreases, due to merging of canonical positions.", "poster_quote": "FPR increases as retained ratio r = m’/m decreases, due to merging of canonical positions."},
    {"id": 28, "text": "Empirical FPR is measured per candidate; only views with FPR ≤ 10% are eligible for selection.", "poster_quote": "Empirical FPR is measured per candidate; only views with FPR ≤ 10% are eligible for selection."},
    {"id": 29, "text": "Channel-aware selection of OR-folded Bloom filters improves communication efficiency and receiver freshness under time-varying channels, especially when opportunities vary substantially (Five-State, Rayleigh).", "poster_quote": "Channel-aware selection of OR-folded Bloom filters improves communication efficiency and receiver freshness under time-varying channels, especially when opportunities vary substantially (Five-State, Rayleigh)."},
    {"id": 30, "text": "Under favorable conditions (Gilbert-Elliott), it remains competitive in efficiency and provides the freshest receiver state.", "poster_quote": "Under favorable conditions (Gilbert-Elliott), it remains competitive in efficiency and provides the freshest receiver state."},
    {"id": 31, "text": "Smaller views trade higher FPR for fresher updates, preserving no-false-negative property.", "poster_quote": "Smaller views trade higher FPR for fresher updates, preserving no-false-negative property."},
    {"id": 32, "text": "This approach is useful when recent, lower-fidelity updates are preferable to delayed, larger ones.", "poster_quote": "This approach is useful when recent, lower-fidelity updates are preferable to delayed, larger ones."},
    {"id": 33, "text": "Future work should address fixed-folded baselines, dynamic contents, and real-world channel conditions.", "poster_quote": "Future work should address fixed-folded baselines, dynamic contents, and real-world channel conditions."}
  ]
